  "Why are analog-to-digital converters (ADC) necessary in embedded systems?\nA. A type=\"button\" class=\"w-full rounded-xl border bg-white px-4 py-3 text-left transition-all cursor-not-allowed border-red-500 bg-red-50/50 shadow-2xs\" disabled> A Because processors can only process analog signals\nB. B type=\"button\" class=\"w-full rounded-xl border bg-white px-4 py-3 text-left transition-all cursor-not-allowed border-green-500 bg-green-50/50 shadow-2xs\" disabled> B Because processors operate with digital signals while real-world signals are often analog\nC. C type=\"button\" class=\"w-full rounded-xl border bg-white px-4 py-3 text-left transition-all cursor-not-allowed border-slate-200 hover:border-primary/50\" disabled> C Because analog signals are faster than digital signals\nD. D type=\"button\" class=\"w-full rounded-xl border bg-white px-4 py-3 text-left transition-all cursor-not-allowed border-slate-200 hover:border-primary/50\" disabled> D Because ADC increases memory capacity\nB",
